{"prompt": {"messages": [{"role": "system", "content": "You are a helpful assistant that translates C++ code to Java 8 code. The code should reads and writes I/O from the console."}, {"role": "user", "content": "Translate the following GNU C++11 code to Java 8 code. The code reads and writes I/O from the console. Your translated code should have the exact same functionality as the given code, meaning that it should have the same output for any given input.\nPrint your translated code and also the confidence score you give to your translation. The confidence score should be a number between 0 and 1. The format of the output should be:\n<translated_code>\n<your_translated_code>\n</translated_code>\n<confidence>\n<your_confidence_score>\n</confidence>\nDo not provide any other text or markdown fences.\n\nHere is the original GNU C++11 code you have to translate:\n<original_code>\n#include <iostream>\n#include <vector>\n#include <set>\nusing namespace std;\n\nusing i64 = long long;\nconst i64 MOD = 1000000007LL;\n\ni64 binpow(i64 a, i64 b, i64 m) {\n    a %= m;\n    i64 res = 1;\n    while (b > 0) {\n        if (b & 1) res = res * a % m;\n        a = a * a % m;\n        b >>= 1;\n    }\n    return res;\n}\n\nclass UnionFind {\npublic:\n    vector<int> parent;\n    vector<int> size;\n    \n    UnionFind(int n) : parent(n+1), size(n+1, 1) {\n        for (int i = 1; i <= n; ++i) parent[i] = i;\n    }\n    \n    int find(int x) {\n        if (parent[x] != x) {\n            parent[x] = find(parent[x]);\n        }\n        return parent[x];\n    }\n    \n    void merge(int x, int y) {\n        int rootX = find(x), rootY = find(y);\n        if (rootX == rootY) return;\n        \n        if (size[rootX] < size[rootY]) swap(rootX, rootY);\n        parent[rootY] = rootX;\n        size[rootX] += size[rootY];\n    }\n};\n\nint main() {\n    int P, K;\n    cin >> P >> K;\n    \n    UnionFind uf(P);\n    \n    for (int i = 1; i < P; ++i) {\n        int val = (1LL * K * i) % P;\n        if (val == 0) val = P;\n        uf.merge(i, val);\n    }\n    \n    set<int> roots;\n    for (int i = 1; i <= P; ++i) {\n        roots.insert(uf.find(i));\n    }\n    \n    i64 result;\n    if (K == 0) {\n        result = binpow(P, P - 1, MOD);\n    } else if (K == 1) {\n        result = binpow(P, P, MOD);\n    } else {\n        result = binpow(P, (i64)roots.size(), MOD);\n    }\n    \n    cout << result << endl;\n    \n    return 0;\n}\n</original_code>\n"}], "temp": 0, "sample_size": 1, "logprobs": true, "model": "qwen/qwen3-coder-next"}, "response": {"samples": [{"content": "<translated_code>\nimport java.util.*;\n\npublic class Main {\n    static final long MOD = 1000000007L;\n\n    static long binpow(long a, long b, long m) {\n        a %= m;\n        long res = 1;\n        while (b > 0) {\n            if ((b & 1) == 1) {\n                res = (res * a) % m;\n            }\n            a = (a * a) % m;\n            b >>= 1;\n        }\n        return res;\n    }\n\n    static class UnionFind {\n        int[] parent;\n        int[] size;\n\n        UnionFind(int n) {\n            parent = new int[n + 1];\n            size = new int[n + 1];\n            for (int i = 1; i <= n; ++i) {\n                parent[i] = i;\n                size[i] = 1;\n            }\n        }\n\n        int find(int x) {\n            if (parent[x] != x) {\n                parent[x] = find(parent[x]);\n            }\n            return parent[x];\n        }\n\n        void merge(int x, int y) {\n            int rootX = find(x);\n            int rootY = find(y);\n            if (rootX == rootY) return;\n\n            if (size[rootX] < size[rootY]) {\n                int temp = rootX;\n                rootX = rootY;\n                rootY = temp;\n            }\n            parent[rootY] = rootX;\n            size[rootX] += size[rootY];\n        }\n    }\n\n    public static void main(String[] args) {\n        Scanner scanner = new Scanner(System.in);\n        int P = scanner.nextInt();\n        int K = scanner.nextInt();\n\n        UnionFind uf = new UnionFind(P);\n\n        for (int i = 1; i < P; ++i) {\n            int val = (int) (((long) K * i) % P);\n            if (val == 0) val = P;\n            uf.merge(i, val);\n        }\n\n        Set<Integer> roots = new HashSet<>();\n        for (int i = 1; i <= P; ++i) {\n            roots.add(uf.find(i));\n        }\n\n        long result;\n        if (K == 0) {\n            result = binpow(P, P - 1, MOD);\n        } else if (K == 1) {\n            result = binpow(P, P, MOD);\n        } else {\n            result = binpow(P, (long) roots.size(), MOD);\n        }\n\n        System.out.println(result);\n    }\n}\n</translated_code>\n<confidence>\n0.95\n</confidence>", "token_logprobs": [-0.00013290952483657748, -1.6689286894688848e-06, -2.3841855067985307e-07, -0.0007351318490691483, -4.1960789531003684e-05, -0.009767713956534863, -0.16035835444927216, -5.364274329622276e-05, -1.1920922133867862e-06, -7.593343616463244e-05, -0.0011709030950441957, -0.0001586549769854173, -0.1614033430814743, -0.0003651905863080174, -0.00012230125139467418, -2.9802276912960224e-06, 0.0, 0.0, -4.768370445162873e-07, -2.753696753643453e-05, 0.0, -1.1920928244535389e-07, -4.172316494077677e-06, 0.0, 0.0, -9.536738616588991e-07, 0.0, -4.541770613286644e-05, -0.001065163523890078, -0.04858766868710518, -2.3841855067985307e-07, -0.0005557184922508895, -0.00023576818057335913, -2.7418097943154862e-06, -2.6464111215318553e-05, -2.062299427052494e-05, -1.1920928244535389e-07, -1.1920928244535389e-07, -1.6689286894688848e-06, -1.1920928244535389e-07, -1.2993727978027891e-05, -5.960446742392378e-06, 0.0, -8.344646857949556e-07, 0.0, -2.2411095415009186e-05, -5.960462772236497e-07, -1.0728830375228426e-06, 0.0, -3.3378546504536644e-06, -4.136476854910143e-05, -2.622600959512056e-06, -3.576278118089249e-07, 0.0, 0.0, 0.0, -1.3470558769768104e-05, 0.0, -8.344646857949556e-07, 0.0, 0.0, -3.576278118089249e-07, 0.0, -1.192092824453